Here's a patch that should fix it.  Tested in ASCII mode (because I
don't have the right dev files around to compile tiles mode).

http://www.potatojunkie.co.uk/hacks/nethack-3.4.3-pilesize.1.diff

The "pilesize" compound option sets the maximum number of objects that
will be included in the "Things that are here" list.  If any more
objects than that are present, you will instead get the "There are
several objects here." message.  The minimum value allowed is 1, which
will tell you about one object ("You see here ...") and will never give
you the "Things that are here" list.

Note that it's not a plain interface patch, as (like customizable
autopickup) it reduces the chance of succumbing to one of the many
'trice-corpse-related accidents.

